<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gottschalk (Obotrite prince)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1066</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gottschalk was a prince of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/obotrites">Obotrites</a> in the mid-11th century who built a large realm among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a> of present-day Mecklenburg and Holstein. Raised as a Christian, he worked with Archbishop Adalbert of Hamburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bremen">Bremen</a> to found churches and bishoprics among his people. He was killed in a pagan uprising at Lenzen in June 1066, which drove out the clergy and German influence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gottschalk-obotrite-prince.jpg" alt="Gottschalk (Obotrite prince)" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: BonifatiusSecuris · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saint_Gottschalk_of_the_Obotrites.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
